---
layout: layouts/piece.njk
title: "The Café — Who We Are Post (1080 × 1080)"
canvasW: "1080px"
canvasH: "1080px"
pageCss: "/assets/css/fb-who-we-are.css"

# ── EDIT THIS ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# The body copy, one string per paragraph. Three short paragraphs is
# what the card is measured for — a fourth will push the date block
# into the footer. The long version belongs in the Facebook caption,
# not on the image: feed crops the picture, never the caption.
#
# Write & as a literal, never &amp; — Nunjucks escapes these on output.
story:
  - "We have cooked on 6th Street since 2005 — scratch breakfast, lunch, and catering for our neighbors."
  - "On Monday we open our doors with an all-new menu, made the way we would feed our own families."

# The line that keeps the promise honest. This post deliberately does
# NOT say grand opening: the kitchen is still coming off years of one
# kind of cooking, and a new menu takes a while to settle. Say the
# quiet part out loud rather than over-promise and under-deliver.
modestLine: "Not a grand opening — just open. A brand new menu takes a while to settle, and we would rather get it right than get it loud. The celebration comes later."

# The caption. Shown on /studio/downloads/ with a copy button.
#
# NOTE: this post and fb-opening-day now tell overlapping stories — the
# opening post's caption carries the Abernathy Building history and the
# Meals on Wheels transition in full. Post one or the other, or space
# them well apart and cut this caption down to the first paragraph.
caption:
  - "Some of you have known us for twenty years. Some of you have never been inside. Either way — hello."
  - "The Café has cooked for Leavenworth since 2005. On Monday, October 5th we open our doors again with an all-new menu: scratch breakfast from 6, lunch through 2, Monday through Friday. Catering and prepared meals carry on the same as always."
  - "We are calling it an opening, not a grand opening. A whole new menu takes a while to settle, and we would rather get it right than get it loud. Come sit down, tell us what you think, and watch it grow with us."
  - "417 S 6th St, Leavenworth · Mon–Fri, 6am–2pm · (913) 547-9994 · lvcafetogo.com"

# Date, hours and address come from the opening block in
# src/_data/site.json, same as the door banner. One edit moves them all.
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

tags: studio
studioTitle: "Who We Are — Facebook post"
studioCategory: "Social"
studioSize: "1080 × 1080 px · square feed post"
studioNote: "The introduce-ourselves post, announcing October 5th as an opening and NOT a grand opening. Body copy is the `story:` list at the top of the .njk; keep it to two or three short paragraphs and put the long version in the Facebook caption instead. Export to PNG and upload — a square post is never cropped in feed."
studioW: 1080
studioH: 1080
studioOrder: 22
---
{# Cream ground, not the teal of fb-opening-day.njk.

   That post is one fact set large; this one is a paragraph of reading. Body
   copy reversed out of a dark ground is measurably slower to read, and this
   audience skews older — so the card is bare stock with a single teal
   masthead, and the teal is spent on the identity instead of the ground.
   The two still read as the same account because the masthead is identical. #}
<div class="canvas whois">

    <header class="whois-mast">
        {# .wordmark--hero, not the print weight: this is a dark composited
           ground at screen size, which is the hero's situation exactly. #}
        <div class="wordmark wordmark--light wordmark--hero whois-wordmark">
            {% inlineSvg "/assets/thecafe.svg", "", site.name %}
        </div>
        <p class="p-eyebrow whois-kicker">Who we are</p>
    </header>

    <section class="whois-body">
        <p class="p-display-italic whois-lede ink-teal">A Leavenworth kitchen<br>since {{ site.founded.slice(0, 4) }}</p>

        <div class="whois-filigree ink-teal">
            {% include "partials/filigree.njk" %}
        </div>

        {%- for para in story %}
        <p class="p-body whois-para">{{ para }}</p>
        {%- endfor %}

        {# The date block. Red on cream is 5.08:1 and passes AA — this is the
           one place on the card the accent is spent, because the date is the
           single thing a reader has to leave with. #}
        <div class="whois-date">
            <p class="p-label whois-date-label ink-accent">Doors open</p>
            <p class="p-display whois-date-line ink-teal">{{ site.opening.dayName }}, {{ site.opening.monthDay }}<sup>{{ site.opening.ordinal }}</sup></p>
            <p class="p-body whois-date-hours ink-teal">
                {{ site.opening.opens.time }}<span class="ampm">{{ site.opening.opens.meridiem }}</span>
                &ndash;
                {{ site.opening.closes.time }}<span class="ampm">{{ site.opening.closes.meridiem }}</span>
                <span class="dot">&middot;</span>
                {{ site.opening.hoursDays }}
            </p>
        </div>

        <p class="p-body whois-modest">{{ modestLine }}</p>
    </section>

    <footer class="whois-foot">
        <p class="p-label foot-line">{{ site.address.street }} <span class="dot">&middot;</span> {{ site.address.locality }}, {{ site.address.region }}</p>
        <p class="p-label foot-line foot-line--quiet">{{ site.social.website }} <span class="dot">&middot;</span> {{ site.phone }}</p>
    </footer>

</div>
